foundation:ErrorHandler foundation:aiBehaviorRules "An ErrorHandler routes a FlowNode's exception (unexpected failure) to a designated fallbackNode instead of failing the entire workflow.\n\nHow to create:\n  assert_individual(class_iri: 'foundation:ErrorHandler', label: '...', properties: [\n    {property_iri: 'foundation:appliesTo',  values: ['<flowNodeIri>']},\n    {property_iri: 'foundation:fallbackNode', values: ['<fallbackNodeIri>']},\n    {property_iri: 'foundation:hasStatus', values: ['foundation:Status_1773183515321']}\n  ])\n\nRules:\n- appliesTo must point to a foundation:automation_FlowNode individual\n- fallbackNode must point to a node that comes AFTER the failing node in the BFS execution order\n- The fallbackNode receives the same ExecutionContext as the failing node (including inputIRIs)\n- Only one ErrorHandler per FlowNode is supported — the first one found wins\n- ErrorHandlers only activate on exceptions, not on outputIRIs='failed' (use a Gateway for that)"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
foundation:ErrorHandler foundation:hasIcon foundation:icon-material-symbols-name-error .
foundation:ErrorHandler foundation:lastUpdatedAt "2026-03-07T17:56:13Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
foundation:ErrorHandler rdf:type owl:Class .
foundation:ErrorHandler rdfs:comment "Defines error handling behavior for a FlowNode. Specifies retry logic, fallback actions, and error recovery strategies."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
foundation:ErrorHandler rdfs:label "Error Handler"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
foundation:ErrorHandler rdfs:subClassOf foundation:AbstractContinuant .
foundation:ErrorHandler rdfs:subClassOf _:restriction_7e880818be9b9c61 .
