unit:ARCSEC <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "\"Arc Second\" is a unit of angular measure, also called the $\\textit{second of arc}$, equal to $1/60 \\; arcminute$. One arcsecond is a very small angle: there are 1,296,000 in a circle. The SI recommends $\\textit{double prime}$ ($''$) as the symbol for the arcsecond. The symbol has become common in astronomy, where very small angles are stated in milliarcseconds ($mas$)."^^<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString> .
