unit:AT <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The $\\textit{ampere-turn}$ was the MKS unit of magnetomotive force (MMF), represented by a direct current of one ampere flowing in a single-turn loop in a vacuum. \"Turns\" refers to the winding number of an electrical conductor comprising an inductor. The ampere-turn was replaced by the SI unit, $ampere$."^^<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString> .
