unit:BIT <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "In information theory, a bit is the amount of information that, on average, can be stored in a discrete bit. It is thus the amount of information carried by a choice between two equally likely outcomes. One bit corresponds to about 0.693 nats (ln(2)), or 0.301 hartleys (log10(2))."^^<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML> .
