unit:BQ-PER-KiloGM foundation:lastUpdatedAt "2026-03-04T04:10:29Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
unit:BQ-PER-KiloGM <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The only unit in the category of Specific radioactivity. It is also known as becquerels per kilogram, becquerel/kilogram. This unit is commonly used in the SI unit system. Becquerel Per Kilogram (Bq/kg) has a dimension of $M{-1}T{-1}$ where $M$ is mass, and $T$ is time. It essentially the same as the corresponding standard SI unit $/kg/s$."^^<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString> .
