unit:BQ-PER-KiloGM qudt:plainTextDescription "\"Becquerel per Kilogram\" is used to describe radioactivity, which is often expressed in becquerels per unit of volume or weight, to express how much radioactive material is contained in a sample."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
