unit:BTU_TH-PER-LB <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "${\\bf Btu_{th} / lbm}$, British Thermal Unit (therm.) Per Pound Mass, is a unit in the category of Thermal heat capacity. It is also known as Btu per pound, Btu/pound, Btu/lb. This unit is commonly used in the UK unit system. British Thermal Unit (therm.) Per Pound Mass (Btu (therm.)/lbm) has a dimension of $L^2T^{-2}$ where $L$ is length, and $T$ is time. It can be converted to the corresponding standard SI unit J/kg by multiplying its value by a factor of 2324.443861."^^<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString> .
