unit:DEGREE_BAUME qudt:plainTextDescription "graduation of the areometer scale for determination of densitiy of fluids.\n\nThe Baumé scale is a pair of hydrometer scales developed by French pharmacist Antoine Baumé in 1768 to measure density of various liquids. The unit of the Baumé scale has been notated variously as degrees Baumé, B°, Bé° and simply Baumé (the accent is not always present). One scale measures the density of liquids heavier than water and the other, liquids lighter than water. The Baumé of distilled water is 0. The API gravity scale is based on errors in early implementations of the Baumé scale."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
