unit:FM <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The $\\textit{fermi}$, or $\\textit{femtometer}$ (other spelling $femtometre$, symbol $fm$) is an SI unit of length equal to $10^{-15} metre$. This distance is often encountered in nuclear physics as a characteristic of this scale. The symbol for the fermi is also $fm$."^^<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString> .
