unit:GT qudt:latexDefinition "${ GT=V\\times (0.2+0.02\\times \\log _{10}(V))}$ where V is measured in cubic meters."^^<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString> .
unit:GT qudt:plainTextDescription "Gross tonnage (GT, G.T. or gt) is a nonlinear measure of a ship's overall internal volume. Gross tonnage is different from gross register tonnage. Gross tonnage is used to determine things such as a ship's manning regulations, safety rules, registration fees, and port dues, whereas the older gross register tonnage is a measure of the volume of only certain enclosed spaces."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
unit:GT qudt:symbol "G.T."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
unit:GT qudt:ucumCode "t{gross}"^^<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/UCUMcs> .
