unit:LB-PER-HR <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Pound per hour is a mass flow unit. It is abbreviated as PPH or more conventionally as lb/h. Fuel flow for engines is usually expressed using this unit, it is particularly useful when dealing with gases or liquids as volume flow varies more with temperature and pressure. $1 lb/h = 0.4535927 kg/h = 126.00 mg/s$.  Minimum fuel intake on a jumbojet can be as low as 150 lb/h when idling, however this is not enough to sustain flight."^^<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString> .
