unit:MHO_Stat <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "\"StatMHO\" is the unit of conductance, admittance, and susceptance in the C.G.S e.s.u system of units. One $statmho$ is the conductance between two points in a conductor when a constant potential difference of $1 \\; statvolt$ applied between the points produces in the conductor a current of $1 \\; statampere$, the conductor not being the source of any electromotive force, approximately $1.1126 \\times 10^{-12} mho$."^^<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString> .
