unit:MegaBIT-PER-SEC <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "A megabit per second (Mbit/s or Mb/s; not to be confused with mbit/s which means millibit per second, or with Mbitps which means megabit picosecond) is a unit of data transfer rate equal to 1,000,000 bits per second or 1,000 kilobits per second or 125,000 bytes per second or 125 kilobytes per second."^^<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML> .
