unit:MicroCi foundation:lastUpdatedAt "2026-03-04T04:10:29Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
unit:MicroCi <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Another commonly used measure of radioactivity, the microcurie: $1 \\micro Ci = 3.7 \\times 10 disintegrations per second = 2.22 \\times 10 disintegrations per minute$. A radiotherapy machine may have roughly 1000 Ci of a radioisotope such as caesium-137 or cobalt-60. This quantity of radioactivity can produce serious health effects with only a few minutes of close-range, un-shielded exposure. The typical human body contains roughly $0.1\\micro Ci$ of naturally occurring potassium-40. "^^<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString> .
unit:MicroCi qudt:applicableSystem <http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/CGS> .
