unit:N <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The \"Newton\" is the SI unit of force. A force of one newton will accelerate a mass of one kilogram at the rate of one meter per second per second. The newton is named for Isaac Newton (1642-1727), the British mathematician, physicist, and natural philosopher. He was the first person to understand clearly the relationship between force (F), mass (m), and acceleration (a) expressed by the formula $F = m \\cdot a$."^^<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString> .
