unit:N-PER-C <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Newton Per Coulomb ( N/C) is a unit in the category of Electric field strength. It is also known as newtons/coulomb. Newton Per Coulomb ( N/C) has a dimension of MLT-3I-1 where $M$ is mass, $L$ is length, $T$ is time, and $I$ is electric current. It essentially the same as the corresponding standard SI unit V/m."^^<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML> .
