unit:PER-PlanckMass2 qudt:latexDefinition "$m_P = \\sqrt{\\frac{ \\hbar c^3}{G}} \\approx 1.2209 \\times 10^{19} GeV/c^2 = 2.17651(13) \\times 10^{-8}$, where $c$ is the speed of light in a vacuum, $\\hbar$ is the reduced Planck's constant, and $G$ is the gravitational constant. The two digits enclosed by parentheses are the estimated standard error associated with the reported numerical value."^^<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString> .
