unit:PERM_Metric <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "A perm is a unit of permeance or \"water vapor transmission\" given a certain differential in partial pressures on either side of a material or membrane. The metric perm (not an SI unit) is defined as 1 gram of water vapor per day, per square metre, per millimeter of mercury."@en .
