unit:PERM_US <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "A perm is a unit of permeance or \"water vapor transmission\" given a certain differential in partial pressures on either side of a material or membrane. The U.S. perm is defined as 1 grain of water vapor per hour, per square foot, per inch of mercury."@en .
