unit:PlanckEnergy foundation:lastUpdatedAt "2026-03-04T04:10:29Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
unit:PlanckEnergy <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "In physics, the unit of energy in the system of natural units known as Planck units is called the Planck energy, denoted by $E_P$. $E_P$ is a derived, as opposed to basic, Planck unit. An equivalent definition is:$E_P = \\hbar / T_P$ where $T_P$ is the Planck time. Also: $E_P = m_P c^2$ where $m_P$ is the Planck mass."^^<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString> .
unit:PlanckEnergy qudt:applicableSystem <http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/PLANCK> .
unit:PlanckEnergy qudt:conversionMultiplier "1956100000"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal> .
