unit:PlanckImpedance foundation:lastUpdatedAt "2026-03-04T04:10:29Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
unit:PlanckImpedance <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The Planck impedance is the unit of electrical resistance, denoted by ZP, in the system of natural units known as Planck units. The Planck impedance is directly coupled to the impedance of free space, Z0, and differs in value from Z0 only by a factor of $4\\pi$. If the Planck charge were instead defined to normalize the permittivity of free space, $\\epsilon_0$, rather than the Coulomb constant, $1/(4\\pi\\epsilon_0)$, then the Planck impedance would be identical to the characteristic impedance of free space."^^<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString> .
unit:PlanckImpedance qudt:applicableSystem <http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/PLANCK> .
unit:PlanckImpedance qudt:conversionMultiplier "29.9792458"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal> .
unit:PlanckImpedance qudt:conversionMultiplierSN "29.9792458"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal> .
unit:PlanckImpedance qudt:derivedUnitOfSystem <http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/PLANCK> .
unit:PlanckImpedance qudt:hasDimensionVector <http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E-2L2I0M1H0T-3D0> .
unit:PlanckImpedance qudt:hasQuantityKind <http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Resistance> .
unit:PlanckImpedance qudt:informativeReference "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Planck_impedance"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
unit:PlanckImpedance qudt:latexDefinition "$Z_P = \\frac{V_P}{I_P}= \\frac{1}{4\\pi\\epsilon_0c}=\\frac{\\mu_oc}{4\\pi}=\\frac{Z_0}{4\\pi}=29.9792458\\Omega$\\where $V_P$ is the Planck voltage, $I_P$ is the Planck current, $c$ is the speed of light in a vacuum, $\\epsilon_0$ is the permittivity of free space, $\\mu_0$ is the permeability of free space, and $Z_0$ is the impedance of free space."^^<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString> .
unit:PlanckImpedance qudt:symbol "Zₚ"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
unit:PlanckImpedance rdf:type qudt:Unit .
unit:PlanckImpedance rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://qudt.org/2.1/vocab/unit> .
unit:PlanckImpedance rdfs:label "Planck Impedance"@en .
unit:PlanckLength foundation:lastUpdatedAt "2026-03-04T04:10:29Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
unit:PlanckLength <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "In physics, the Planck length, denoted $\\ell_P$, is a unit of length, equal to $1.616199(97)×10^{-35}$ metres. It is a base unit in the system of Planck units. The Planck length can be defined from three fundamental physical constants: the speed of light in a vacuum, Planck's constant, and the gravitational constant. "^^<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString> .
unit:PlanckLength qudt:applicableSystem <http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/PLANCK> .
unit:PlanckLength qudt:conversionMultiplier "0.00000000000000000000000000000000001616252"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal> .
unit:PlanckLength qudt:conversionMultiplierSN "0.00000000000000000000000000000000001616252"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal> .
unit:PlanckLength qudt:dbpediaMatch "http://dbpedia.org/resource/Planck_length"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
unit:PlanckLength qudt:hasDimensionVector <http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L1I0M0H0T0D0> .
unit:PlanckLength qudt:hasQuantityKind <http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Length> .
unit:PlanckLength qudt:informativeReference "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Planck_length?oldid=495093067"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
unit:PlanckLength qudt:informativeReference "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Planck_units"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
unit:PlanckLength qudt:latexDefinition "$\\ell_P = \\sqrt{\\frac{ \\hbar G}{c^3}} \\approx 1.616199(97)) \\times 10^{-35} m$, where $c$ is the speed of light in a vacuum, $\\hbar$ is the reduced Planck's constant, and $G$ is the gravitational constant. The two digits enclosed by parentheses are the estimated standard error associated with the reported numerical value."^^<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString> .
unit:PlanckLength qudt:latexSymbol "$\\ell_P$"^^<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString> .
unit:PlanckLength qudt:symbol "plancklength"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
unit:PlanckLength rdf:type qudt:Unit .
unit:PlanckLength rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://qudt.org/2.1/vocab/unit> .
unit:PlanckLength rdfs:label "Planck Length"@en .
unit:PlanckMass foundation:lastUpdatedAt "2026-03-04T04:10:29Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
unit:PlanckMass <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "In physics, the Planck mass, denoted by $m_P$, is the unit of mass in the system of natural units known as Planck units. It is defined so that $\\approx  1.2209 \\times 10 GeV/c_0 = 2.17651(13) \\times 10 kg$, (or $21.7651 \\mu g$), where $c_0$ is the speed of light in a vacuum, $G$ is the gravitational constant, and $\\hbar$ is the reduced Planck constant. Particle physicists and cosmologists often use the reduced Planck mass, which is $\\approx  4.341 \\times 10 kg = 2.435  \\times 10 GeV/c$. The added factor of $1/{\\sqrt{8\\pi}}$ simplifies a number of equations in general relativity. Quantum effects are typified by the magnitude of Planck's constant."^^<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString> .
unit:PlanckMass qudt:applicableSystem <http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/PLANCK> .
unit:PlanckMass qudt:conversionMultiplier "0.0000000217644"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal> .
unit:PlanckMass qudt:conversionMultiplierSN "0.0000000217644"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal> .
unit:PlanckMass qudt:dbpediaMatch "http://dbpedia.org/resource/Planck_mass"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
unit:PlanckMass qudt:hasDimensionVector <http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M1H0T0D0> .
unit:PlanckMass qudt:hasQuantityKind <http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Mass> .
unit:PlanckMass qudt:informativeReference "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Planck_mass?oldid=493648632"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
unit:PlanckMass qudt:informativeReference "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Planck_units"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
unit:PlanckMass qudt:latexDefinition "$m_P = \\sqrt{\\frac{ \\hbar c^3}{G}} \\approx 1.2209 \\times 10^{19} GeV/c^2 = 2.17651(13) \\times 10^{-8}$, where $c$ is the speed of light in a vacuum, $\\hbar$ is the reduced Planck's constant, and $G$ is the gravitational constant. The two digits enclosed by parentheses are the estimated standard error associated with the reported numerical value."^^<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString> .
unit:PlanckMass qudt:latexSymbol "$m_P$"^^<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString> .
