unit:PlanckPower foundation:lastUpdatedAt "2026-03-04T04:10:29Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
unit:PlanckPower <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The Planck energy divided by the Planck time is the Planck power $P_p $, equal to about $3.62831 \\times 10^{52} W$. This is an extremely large unit; even gamma-ray bursts, the most luminous phenomena known, have output on the order of $1 \\times 10^{45} W$, less than one ten-millionth of the Planck power."^^<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString> .
unit:PlanckPower qudt:applicableSystem <http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/PLANCK> .
unit:PlanckPower qudt:conversionMultiplier "36283100000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal> .
unit:PlanckPower qudt:conversionMultiplierSN "36283100000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal> .
unit:PlanckPower qudt:dbpediaMatch "http://dbpedia.org/resource/Planck_power"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
unit:PlanckPower qudt:derivedUnitOfSystem <http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/PLANCK> .
unit:PlanckPower qudt:hasDimensionVector <http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L2I0M1H0T-3D0> .
unit:PlanckPower qudt:hasQuantityKind <http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Power> .
unit:PlanckPower qudt:informativeReference "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Planck_power?oldid=493642483"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
unit:PlanckPower qudt:latexDefinition "$P_p = {\\frac{ c^5}{G}}$, where $c$ is the speed of light in a vacuum, and $G$ is the gravitational constant."^^<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString> .
