unit:RAD-PER-SEC2 <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Angular acceleration is the rate of change of angular velocity. In SI units, it is measured in radians per Square second ($rad/s^2$), and is usually denoted by the Greek letter $\\alpha$."^^<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString> .
