unit:V-PER-SEC <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "'Volt per Second' is a unit of magnetic flux equaling one weber. This is the flux passing through a conducting loop and reduced to zero at a uniform rate in one second inducing an electric potential of one volt in the loop. "^^<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML> .
