unit:W-PER-M2 <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "\"Watt per Square Meter} is a unit of irradiance defined as the power received per area. This is a unit in the category of Energy flux. It is also known as watts per square meter, watt per square metre, watts per square metre, watt/square meter, watt/square metre. This unit is commonly used in the SI unit system. Watt Per Square Meter ($W/m^2$) has a dimension of $MT^{-3\"$ where $M$ is mass, and $T$ is time. This unit is the standard SI unit in this category."^^<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString> .
