unit:YD2 <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The square yard is an imperial/US customary unit of area, formerly used in most of the English-speaking world but now generally replaced by the square metre outside of the U.S. , Canada and the U.K. It is defined as the area of a square with sides of one yard in length. (Gaj in Hindi)."^^<http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML> .
